Changes relative to Freerouting
-------------------------------
- Complete translation from Java to Rust. With --parity the output is
  byte-identical to Freerouting's deterministic mode on its benchmark boards.
- Parallel optimizer and parallel autorouting passes, multi-start routing,
  checkpoints, --max-time and stop signals, progress reporting.
- Many routing fixes and enhancements (see docs/IMPROVEMENTS.md), among them:
  plane connections, class-pair clearances, minimum track width for neck-down,
  rollback of bad passes, stagnation stops, optimizer time budgets.
- New features: length matching (--tune), controlled-impedance widths and
  no-neckdown classes, differential pair routing (--pairs).
- A KiCad plugin (integrations/kicad) with design-rule translation from
  .kicad_dru, impedance calculator and length/pair rules.

Test data
---------
crates/*/testdata contains boards and sessions derived from the Freerouting
test fixtures and benchmark boards (GPL-3.0, from the Freerouting repository)
and from KiCad demo projects.

